IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa2-pay`

-- Cases for fwa2-pay.l4. Every expected value was worked by hand from the text (section cited), not copied from the
-- encoding's output. Edges: exactly 38 hours; leave counted in the week; paid on the due day and a day late; exactly
-- one month between pay days; the underpayment just below and above the penalty-unit floor; the penalty unit's
-- indexation day.

§ `s 62 -- maximum weekly hours`

-- Full-time: 38 (s 62(1)(a)). Part-time on 20 ordinary hours: the lesser of 38 and 20 = 20; on 40: 38 (s 62(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `How many hours a week before extra hours must be reasonable` TRUE 0 EQUALS 38
#ASSERT `How many hours a week before extra hours must be reasonable` FALSE 20 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many hours a week before extra hours must be reasonable` FALSE 40 EQUALS 38

-- Exactly 38 hours: not "more than" 38, so s 62 gives no right to refuse and says nothing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` TRUE 0 38 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 39 hours, unreasonable: may refuse (s 62(2)).
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` TRUE 0 39 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 39 hours, reasonable: no right to refuse.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` TRUE 0 39 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part-time on 20 ordinary hours, asked for 16 hours in a week with 8 hours of authorised leave: 24 counted (s 62(4)), over 20.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` FALSE 20 16 8 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same week without the leave: 16, under 20: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` FALSE 20 16 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A full-time junior hospital doctor rostered 60 hours, the extra 22 found unreasonable: may refuse, and the employer is in breach.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse these additional hours` TRUE 0 60 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my employer breaking the maximum hours rule` TRUE 0 60 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same 60 hours found reasonable (the s 62(3) weighing went the other way): no breach.
#ASSERT `Is my employer breaking the maximum hours rule` TRUE 0 60 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my employer breaking the maximum hours rule` TRUE 0 38 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 323 -- paid in full and on time`

-- Pay period ending 14 January 2026, due 21 January. Paid 1,000 of 1,000 on 21 January (the due day): in time.
#ASSERT `Was I paid in full by the due day` (Date 14 1 2026) (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 21 1 2026) 1000 1000
-- Paid the full amount a day late, on 22 January: breach.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I paid in full by the due day` (Date 14 1 2026) (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) 1000 1000)
-- Paid early but 900 of 1,000: not in full.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I paid in full by the due day` (Date 14 1 2026) (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 20 1 2026) 1000 900)
-- Paid 1,100 on time: in full.
#ASSERT `Was I paid in full by the due day` (Date 14 1 2026) (Date 21 1 2026) (Date 19 1 2026) 1000 1100

-- Paid by transfer, nothing specified, 15 January then 15 February 2026: exactly one month, complies.
#ASSERT `Does the way I am paid comply` `a transfer into an account I hold` FALSE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 2 2026)
-- 16 February: more than a month (s 323(1)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the way I am paid comply` `a transfer into an account I hold` FALSE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 16 2 2026))
-- Paid in vouchers: not money by a s 323(2) method.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the way I am paid comply` `goods, vouchers or credit, or into someone else's account` FALSE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 29 1 2026))
-- Cash, but the award specifies transfer and the employer did not use it (s 323(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the way I am paid comply` `cash` TRUE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 29 1 2026))
#ASSERT `Does the way I am paid comply` `cash` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 29 1 2026)

§ `ss 324, 326 -- deductions`

-- Arguments: written; states amount; my benefit; employer benefit; varies; regs reasonable; EA; award/FWC; law/court;
-- under a term; unreasonable; age; parent agreed.
-- Salary sacrifice I authorised in writing, for my benefit: permitted (s 324(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Is this deduction permitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE
-- Written and for my benefit but also for the employer's, in a varying amount, not prescribed reasonable: s 324(1A) bars it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this deduction permitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE)
-- The same, prescribed as reasonable: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this deduction permitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE
-- Written authority that does not state the amount (s 324(2)(a)): not authorised.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this deduction permitted` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE)
-- No authority of any kind (a till shortfall taken from pay): not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this deduction permitted` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 FALSE)
-- Tax withheld under a law: permitted (s 324(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Is this deduction permitted` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE
-- An award term permitting an unreasonable deduction for the employer's benefit: the term has no effect (s 326(1)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this deduction permitted` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 30 FALSE)
-- A 16-year-old's deduction made under a contract term, no parent's written agreement: no effect (s 326(4)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this deduction permitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 16 FALSE)
-- The same with a parent's written agreement: permitted.
#ASSERT `Is this deduction permitted` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 16 TRUE

§ `s 325 -- being made to spend or pay`

-- Arguments: prospective; payment; unreasonable; benefits employer.
-- Employee made to spend unreasonably (uniform from a set supplier): unlawful; (b) applies only to payments.
#ASSERT `Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Employee made to pay, unreasonable, but no benefit to the employer or a related party: not s 325(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Employee made to pay the employer unreasonably (cash-back): unlawful.
#ASSERT `Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A reasonable requirement: not unlawful.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Job applicant made to spend unreasonably, no benefit to the employer: s 325(1A)(c) not met (the reading in NOTES.md finding 3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Job applicant made to pay for an unpaid "trial" placement to a related company: unlawful.
#ASSERT `Is the requirement to spend or pay unlawful` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 546A, 327A(7) -- the underpayment`

#ASSERT `How much was I underpaid` 5000 3200 EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `How much was I underpaid` 5000 6000 EQUALS 0
-- 10 overtime hours at 60.00, nothing paid: 600. A junior doctor's 120 hours at 75.50 = 9,060, paid 2,000: 7,060.
#ASSERT `How much am I owed for unpaid overtime` 10 60 0 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `How much am I owed for unpaid overtime` 120 75.50 2000 EQUALS 7060

§ `s 327A -- the offence`

-- Arguments: required; kind; referral extension only; not paid in full by due day; intention; after commencement.
#ASSERT `Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `wages or other pay` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Superannuation, where the national system reaches us only by a State referral extension: excluded (s 327A(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `superannuation contributions` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Superannuation with no referral extension: not excluded.
#ASSERT `Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `superannuation contributions` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Wages under a referral extension: (2)(b) does not list wages, so not excluded.
#ASSERT `Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `wages or other pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No intention proved: no offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `wages or other pay` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Conduct before the offence commenced (Sch 1 cl 98): no offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my employer committed the wage theft offence` TRUE `wages or other pay` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Penalty unit $364 from 1 July 2026. Individual: 5,000 units = 1,820,000. Body corporate: 25,000 units = 9,100,000.
-- Individual, underpayment 1,000,000: 3 times = 3,000,000 > 1,820,000.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` TRUE 1000000 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 3000000
-- Individual, underpayment 100,000: 300,000 < 1,820,000.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` TRUE 100000 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1820000
-- Edge: 606,667 x 3 = 1,820,001, just over the floor; 606,666 x 3 = 1,819,998, just under.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` TRUE 606667 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1820001
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` TRUE 606666 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1820000
-- Body corporate, underpayment 1,000,000: 3,000,000 < 9,100,000.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `a body corporate` TRUE 1000000 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 9100000
-- Body corporate, underpayment 4,000,000 over a course of conduct: 12,000,000.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `a body corporate` TRUE 4000000 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 12000000
-- The court cannot determine the underpayment: the penalty units alone (s 327A(6)(b)).
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` FALSE 4000000 (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1820000
-- On the indexation day itself: $364 applies. The day before: the dollar value is not in the deposit, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` FALSE 0 (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST 1820000
#ASSERT `What is the largest wage theft fine` `an individual` FALSE 0 (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the longest wage theft prison term` `an individual` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `What is the longest wage theft prison term` `a body corporate` EQUALS 0

§ `s 545A -- casual loading set off`

-- Described as casual, loading 2,000, in fact permanent, claim 5,000, full set-off: 3,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my claim is left after the casual loading` TRUE 2000 TRUE 5000 1 EQUALS 3000
-- Claim 1,500 less loading 2,000: not below nil.
#ASSERT `How much of my claim is left after the casual loading` TRUE 2000 TRUE 1500 1 EQUALS 0
-- The court sets off half the loading (s 545A(3)): 5,000 - 1,000 = 4,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my claim is left after the casual loading` TRUE 2000 TRUE 5000 0.5 EQUALS 4000
-- In fact a casual: s 545A does not apply, the claim stands.
#ASSERT `How much of my claim is left after the casual loading` TRUE 2000 FALSE 5000 1 EQUALS 5000
